48747.3 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=116 triangles=84774 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 116 visible materials / 84774 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
48747.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=116 triangles=84774 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 116 visible materials / 84774 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
48747.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=52 visible=49 resolved=52 missing=0 materials=49 triangles=54879 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=NATURE/BLENDCLIFFTOGRASS_ODYSSEY resource=materials/Nature/rockwall003_height-ssbump.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 49 visible materials that name one of 28 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
48747.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=refused declared=5 visible=5 resolved=5 missing=0 materials=5 triangles=13706 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=NATURE/BLENDCLIFFTOGRASS_ODYSSEY resource=materials/nature/dirtground001_height-ssbump.vtf reason=$bumpmap2 is layer 2's normal map: it is lerped into layer 1's normal by the vertex blend weight, so it is sampled only when --world-material-bump and --world-bump2 are both on; with either off it is refused, not silently replaced by layer 1's; 4/5 of those materials also declare $ssbump, so their second-layer texel is a bumpBasis weight and stays refused even with both switches on (--world-bump2-texture measures the layer with a diagnostic normal map instead)
48747.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=15 visible=14 resolved=0 missing=15 materials=14 triangles=19310 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=WOOD/WALL007A resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 15 of 15 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; 1 material names a %detailtype group (first=tf_forest_grass); %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
48747.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=$ssbump kind=material-key state=refused declared=36 visible=35 resolved=36 missing=0 materials=35 triangles=48658 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=NATURE/BLENDCLIFFTOGRASS_ODYSSEY resource=Nature/rockwall003_height-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
